# Human accept checklist

Before approving an agent-authored PR, check:

- [ ] Risk tier matches reality — re-read the diff if it's tagged "trivial" but
      touches shared state, auth, or external calls.
- [ ] Impact report's `open_questions` are resolved, not just acknowledged.
- [ ] Spec diff reads correctly on its own — would a new team member understand
      the change from the spec alone?
- [ ] Test diff only adds/extends, never removes or weakens assertions.
- [ ] CI passed on the actual updated tests (not stale/skipped ones).
- [ ] No new dependency added without a reason stated in the PR description.
- [ ] Nothing in "things to never touch" (CLAUDE.md) was touched.

If risk_tier is `needs-deep-review`: read the full diff line by line, not just
the aggregated comment.
